  "summary": "vercel-runtime-python exfiltrates host identity to webhook.site collector",
  "details": "Package name impersonates Vercel's Python runtime. index.py defines send_device_info() which collects os.getlogin(), os.getcwd(), the local hostname, and the local IP address and POSTs them as JSON to a hardcoded webhook.site endpoint (https://webhook.site/f9bff304-3053-4d54-be05-86537267514a). __init__.py attempts to re-export this function (from.index import get_device_info, send_info), though the symbol names in the import statement do not match those defined in index.py so a plain `import vercel_runtime_python` raises ImportError; the exfiltration function remains reachable directly as vercel_runtime_python.index.send_device_info. Package metadata is generic (\"Python utility package\", author \"lapin\", version 100.99.99) and the shipped code has no functionality matching the impersonated Vercel Python runtime.",
